{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-psa-138-1","title":"Psalms 138:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":138,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":138,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 David praises God for the truth of his word. 4 He prophesies that the kings of the earth shall praise God. 7 He professes his confidence in God.</p>\n<p>A.M. 3485. B.C. 519. (Title.) A Psalm of David.Five MSS. omit {ledawid;} and the LXX. and Arabic prefix also the names of Haggai and Zechariah; and it is probable that it was composed to be sung at the dedication of the second temple.</p>\n<p>I will praise. 9:1; 86:12,13; 103:1,2; 111:1; 1Co 14:15; Eph 5:19 with my whole.The versions and several MSS. add Jehovah.</p>\n<p>before. 82:1,6; 119:46; Ex 22:28; Joh 10:34-36; Ac 23:5; Heb 1:14 the gods. Or, God. Elohim.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-138-2","title":"Psalms 138:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":138,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":138,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>toward. 5:7; 28:2; 99:5,9; 1Ki 8:29,30; Da 6:10 and praise. 36:5,6; 85:10; 86:15; 89:1,2; 100:4,5; 115:1; Isa 63:7; Mic 7:18-20 Lu 1:68-72; Joh 1:17; Ro 15:8,9 for thou hast. 56:4,10; Isa 42:21; Mt 5:18; 24:35; Joh 10:35</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-138-3","title":"Psalms 138:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":138,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":138,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>In the day. 18:6; 34:4-6; 77:1,2; Isa 65:24 strengthenedst. 27:14; 29:11; 63:8; Isa 12:2; 40:29-31; 41:10; Zec 10:12 2Co 12:8-10; Eph 3:16; 6:10; Php 4:13; Col 1:11; 1Pe 5:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-138-4","title":"Psalms 138:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":138,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":138,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>All the kings. 72:11; 102:15,22; Isa 49:23; 60:3-5,16; Re 11:15; 21:24 when they hear. 22:22,27; 51:13; 69:30-32; 71:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-138-5","title":"Psalms 138:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":138,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":138,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>they shall. Isa 52:7-10; 65:14; 66:10-14; Jer 31:11,12; Zep 3:14,15; Mt 21:5-9 Lu 19:37,38 for great. 21:5; Ex 15:11; 33:18,19; Isa 6:1-3; Mal 1:11; Joh 13:31,32; 17:1 2Co 4:6; Eph 1:6,12; Re 4:11; 5:12-14; 7:12; 19:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-138-6","title":"Psalms 138:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":138,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":138,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>Though. 51:17; 113:5,6; 1Sa 2:7,8; Pr 3:34; Isa 57:15; 66:2; Lu 1:51-53 Lu 14:11; 18:14; Jas 4:6; 1Pe 5:5,6 but the proud. Ex 18:11; Job 40:11,12; Isa 2:11,17; Eze 28:2-9; Da 4:37; 5:20-24 Ac 12:22,23 afar off. 139:2; Mt 25:41; 2Th 1:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-138-7","title":"Psalms 138:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":138,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":138,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>Though I walk. 23:3,4; 41:7,8; 66:10-12; Job 13:15; 19:25,26; Isa 57:16 thou wilt. 71:20,21; 85:6; 119:49,50 thou shalt stretch. 35:1-3; 56:1,2,9; 64:7,8; 77:10; 144:1,2; Isa 5:25; 9:12,17,21 Isa 10:4; Mic 7:8-10 and thy right. 17:7; 18:35; 44:3,5-7; 60:5; Isa 41:10; Ac 2:33</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-138-8","title":"Psalms 138:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":138,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":138,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>perfect. 57:2; Isa 26:12; Jer 32:39,40; Joh 15:2; Ro 5:10; 8:28-30; Php 1:6 1Th 5:24 thy mercy. 100:5; 103:17 forsake. 71:6-9,17,18; Job 10:3,8; 14:15; Isa 42:16; 43:21; 1Pe 1:3-5 1Pe 4:19; Jude 1:1</p>"}]}